    {
      "description": "Currently supported OS for the target host is Linux on x86_64. ARM support from the community.\nSearch xxh shell on Github or Bitbucket or create your shell entrypoint to use another portable shell.",
      "items": [],
      "title": "Shells"
    },
    {
      "description": "Prerun plugins allow you to bring any portable tools, dotfiles, or aliases to your xxh session before running the shell.\nPinned plugins: core (xxh-sudo, xxh-screen, xxh-tmux), dotfiles, docker, python, xxh, vim, zoxide, starship. There is cookiecutter template to create a prerun plugin.",
      "items": [],
      "title": "Prerun plugins"
    },
    {
      "description": "Use instead of when connecting to Linux hosts without changing ssh arguments:\nCommon examples (use to get info about arguments):\nFor reusing arguments and simplifying xxh usage (like shortening to ), there is a config file.\nWhy the plus sign for the xxh arguments? The xxh is using the plus sign for xxh arguments to preserve the ability to use the minus sign for the original ssh arguments. This allows just replacing the first two letters in the command to convert it to the command. Also see the discussion.",
      "items": [],
      "title": "Usage"
    },
